  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "Mila wanted a new school bag because the zip on her old one kept opening.",
      "She found a bright replacement in a shop window.",
      "However, buying it would use almost all the money she had saved."
    ],
    [
      "Her father asked her to check the old bag before deciding.",
      "Its straps were strong, and the material was still of good quality.",
      "Only the zip needed attention."
    ],
    [
      "A repair shop offered an alternative: replace the zip for six dollars.",
      "That amount was much smaller than the price of the new bag.",
      "Mila also asked how long the repair would take, because she needed the bag on Monday."
    ],
    [
      "The shop could finish by Saturday, so she chose the repair.",
      "It was an economical choice for this situation: she could keep a useful bag and spend less money.",
      "Mila did not decide that repairing was always best.",
      "If the straps had been damaged too, she would have needed to compare the choices again."
    ]
  ],
  "translations": [
    "米拉想买一个新书包，因为旧书包的拉链总是自己打开。",
    "她在一家商店的橱窗里看到了一个鲜艳的新款。",
    "然而，买下它几乎要用完她存下的所有钱。",
    "爸爸请她在决定前先检查旧书包。",
    "肩带很结实，材料的质量也仍然很好。",
    "只有拉链需要处理。",
    "一家修理店提供了另一种方案：花六美元换拉链。",
    "这个金额比新书包的价格小得多。",
    "米拉还问了修理需要多久，因为她星期一就要用书包。",
    "店里能在星期六前修好，所以她选择了修理。",
    "在这个情况下，这是一个经济实惠的选择：她既能保留一个有用的书包，又少花钱。",
    "米拉并没有因此认定，修理永远是最好的。",
    "如果肩带也损坏了，她就需要重新比较不同选择。"
  ],
